body:
Unfortunately I've had to resort to doing this for the time being:

```
requirejs: {
      compile: {
        options: {
          baseUrl: '<%= config.jsDir %>',
          mainConfigFile: '<%= config.jsDir %>/config.js',
          name: 'main',
          out: '<%= config.distDir %>/<%= config.jsDir %>/main.js',
          paths: {
            'jquery': 'empty:'
          },
          optimize: 'uglify2',
          generateSourceMaps: true,
          preserveLicenseComments: false,
          onBuildRead: function (id, path, contents) {
              if (id.indexOf('instant-search') === 0) {
                  return contents.replace(/define\(\[\], factory\)/i, 'define("instant-search", [], factory)');
              } else {
                  return contents;
              }
          }
        }
      }
    }
```

I'm doing a string replace on build of instantsearch's define().

Eventually when I migrate to webpack this will be a non-issue, but I wish I could figure out how to make requirejs notice instantsearch and name it appropriately on build.
